    <item>
      <title>Bambu Lab A1 mini cabinet</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/en/article/bambu-lab-a1-mini-cabinet/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 00:00:00 &#43;0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/en/article/bambu-lab-a1-mini-cabinet/</guid>
      <description>After setting up my new Bambu Lab A1 mini, I built a wooden cabinet on wheels for it.</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>The Bambu Lab A1 mini is truly a gem of a printer. Although it has a small print area (180x180x180 mm), it is a very precise printer and very easy to use.</p>
<p>So I decided to build a small cabinet to place it on, one that would have space to store the filament spools.</p>
<h2 id="the-project">The project</h2>
<p>I started with a small sketch on paper, which, for now, remains the quickest method for me when it comes to projects of this scale. Then I went to the BricoFer store near my house, bought two 40x100 cm panels of laminated particleboard, and had them cut so that the edge banding would be visible once assembled.</p>
<p><figure class="article-image">
    <a class="article-image__link" href="/it/article/bambu-lab-a1-mini-cabinet/Mobiletto-progetto.jpg" data-lightbox-image>
        <img
            src="/it/article/bambu-lab-a1-mini-cabinet/Mobiletto-progetto_hu_7734c667a9fc32b6.webp"
            alt="Cabinet Design"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            srcset="/it/article/bambu-lab-a1-mini-cabinet/Mobiletto-progetto_hu_7734c667a9fc32b6.webp 640w"
            sizes="100vw"
            width="747"
            height="1146"
             title="Cabinet Design"
        >
    </a>
    <figcaption>Cabinet Design</figcaption>
</figure>
</p>
<h2 id="working-on">Working on</h2>
<p>With the pieces cut to size, I began assembly. I used angle clamps and a quick-release clamp to hold the cabinet sides in place.</p>
<p><figure class="article-image">
    <a class="article-image__link" href="/it/article/bambu-lab-a1-mini-cabinet/Mobiletto-in-costruzione-05.jpg" data-lightbox-image>
        <img
            src="/it/article/bambu-lab-a1-mini-cabinet/Mobiletto-in-costruzione-05_hu_27e3ba69d39df1e8.webp"
            alt="Cabinet under construction"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            srcset="/it/article/bambu-lab-a1-mini-cabinet/Mobiletto-in-costruzione-05_hu_63fc31968ceea299.webp 640w, /it/article/bambu-lab-a1-mini-cabinet/Mobiletto-in-costruzione-05_hu_27e3ba69d39df1e8.webp 960w"
            sizes="100vw"
            width="1382"
            height="1843"
             title="Cabinet under construction"
        >
    </a>
    <figcaption>Cabinet under construction</figcaption>
</figure>
</p>
<p><figure class="article-image">
    <a class="article-image__link" href="/it/article/bambu-lab-a1-mini-cabinet/Mobiletto-in-costruzione-06.jpg" data-lightbox-image>
        <img
            src="/it/article/bambu-lab-a1-mini-cabinet/Mobiletto-in-costruzione-06_hu_cfd223b6b3a1ae8d.webp"
            alt="Close-up of the clamp"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            srcset="/it/article/bambu-lab-a1-mini-cabinet/Mobiletto-in-costruzione-06_hu_f8fe203ce592e71c.webp 640w, /it/article/bambu-lab-a1-mini-cabinet/Mobiletto-in-costruzione-06_hu_cfd223b6b3a1ae8d.webp 960w"
            sizes="100vw"
            width="1382"
            height="1843"
             title="Close-up of the clamp"
        >
    </a>
    <figcaption>Close-up of the clamp</figcaption>
</figure>
</p>
<p>And finally, I assembled the remaining piece—even though it was shorter than the pieces at the bottom and top—to create a shelf in the middle of the cabinet.</p>
<h2 id="completed">Completed</h2>
<p><figure class="article-image">
    <a class="article-image__link" href="/it/article/bambu-lab-a1-mini-cabinet/Mobiletto-completato-02.jpg" data-lightbox-image>
        <img
            src="/it/article/bambu-lab-a1-mini-cabinet/Mobiletto-completato-02_hu_5857488f50698ac8.webp"
            alt="Cabinet completed"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            srcset="/it/article/bambu-lab-a1-mini-cabinet/Mobiletto-completato-02_hu_c4a88f9f87589853.webp 640w, /it/article/bambu-lab-a1-mini-cabinet/Mobiletto-completato-02_hu_5857488f50698ac8.webp 960w"
            sizes="100vw"
            width="1382"
            height="1843"
             title="Cabinet completed"
        >
    </a>
    <figcaption>Cabinet completed</figcaption>
</figure>
</p>
<p>Finally, my Bambulab A1 Mini has its own cabinet with wheels so I can move it around the house.</p>
<p><figure class="article-image">
    <a class="article-image__link" href="/it/article/bambu-lab-a1-mini-cabinet/Mobiletto-in-opera.jpg" data-lightbox-image>
        <img
            src="/it/article/bambu-lab-a1-mini-cabinet/Mobiletto-in-opera_hu_48cedb0dc81717d2.webp"
            alt="Cabinet in operation"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            srcset="/it/article/bambu-lab-a1-mini-cabinet/Mobiletto-in-opera_hu_3bd9f11c1a52eda7.webp 640w, /it/article/bambu-lab-a1-mini-cabinet/Mobiletto-in-opera_hu_48cedb0dc81717d2.webp 960w"
            sizes="100vw"
            width="1382"
            height="1843"
             title="Cabinet in operation"
        >
    </a>
    <figcaption>Cabinet in operation</figcaption>
</figure>
</p>
<p>And I also added a sort of UPS using a <a href="https://it.bluettipower.eu/products/bluetti-eb3a" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Bluetti EB3A 600W (1200W peak)</a>
 that I can disconnect from the mains so I can move the printer around the house while keeping it powered.</p>
<p>As you can see, I&rsquo;m quite fond of this type of structure, which I also used to build the enclosures for the two Anycubic Kobra S1 Combo printers.</p>
<p>ooOOoo</p>
]]></content:encoded>
